<title>JAPAN: TABLE-JAPAN JUNE CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS UP 55.8%.</title>
<headline>TABLE-JAPAN JUNE CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS UP 55.8%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The surplus in Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, rose 55.8 percent in June from a year earlier to 1.02 trillion yen, the Finance Ministry announced on Friday.</p>
<p>The surplus in merchandise trade alone rose 18.7 percent to 1.1 trillion yen from the same month a year earlier.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the balance of payments figures: (Unadjusted, in bln yen) JUNE	  MAY	YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Current Acct Balance  +1,018.1     +906.8	+653.5</p>
<p> -Goods and Services    +633.6     +412.8	+343.2</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	1,097.3     +927.9	+924.6</p>
<p>	 Exports	   4,002.6    3,984.9     3,560.5</p>
<p>	 Imports	   2,905.3    3,057.0     2,636.0</p>
<p>    Services Balance    -463.7     -515.1	-581.3</p>
<p> -Income Balance	  +468.4     +575.2	+378.3</p>
<p> -Current Transfers	-83.9	-81.2	 -67.9</p>
<p>The following figures show the unadjusted balance in Japan's capital and financial accounts (in billion yen):</p>
<p>				JUNE	    MAY	YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Capital/Financial Acct  -678.4	-830.7     -720.5</p>
<p> -Financial Account     -655.3	-817.1     -698.2</p>
<p>  Direct Investment     -337.3	-233.2     -197.2</p>
<p>  Portfolio Investment  -671.8	+148.9   +1,039.2</p>
<p>  Other Investment	+353.7	-732.8    -1540.2</p>
<p> -Capital Account	  -23.0	- 13.6	-22.3</p>
<p>The following figures show the adjusted balance of payments figures (in billions of yen)</p>
<p>				    JUNE	    MAY</p>
<p>Current Account Balance    +976.0	+1,272.8</p>
<p> -Goods and Services	 +483.4	  +813.0</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	  +1,012.3	+1,380.7</p>
<p>	 Exports		 4029.6	 4,480.8</p>
<p>	 Imports		 3017.3	 3,100.1</p>
<p>    Services Balance	 -528.9	  -567.7</p>
<p> -Income Balance	     +605.2	  +558.7</p>
<p> -Current Transfers	  -112.6	   -98.8</p>
